//Inside the class's own member bodies the bare class name rebinds to
//the type for member-expr qualifiers (the ctor shadow never names a
//receiver). The rebind makes the inside spelling match the outside
//one for the func-handle exception too: `Counter.toString()` inside
//the body looks up toString in class scope (the inherited instance
//method) and rejects instance-method-through-type, instead of riding
//the constructor value's by-name toString.
class Counter {
    public Counter() {}
    public int probe() {
        string s = Counter.toString();
        return 1;
    }
}
int main() { return 0; }
